# 2026: every real number is also a complex one. A function for complex
# arguments then also takes real ones (converted when it is calculated),
# but a variant that fits exactly, like + : real,complex below, is chosen
# first; the conversion is the fallback (fewest conversions wins).
SUBSORT real,complex ATT real2cpx
# 2026: number, the sort of symbolic scalar expressions, above real and
# complex (as Number in Julia). Rules with variables of sort number apply
# to real and complex terms as well, and a function variant on number in a
# pattern also matches its real and complex variants. Terms only become of
# sort number when one of their parts is (like the imaginary unit im of
# inc/integration/base); a term of reals keeps the real variants. number has
# no values of its own (no ATT): a numerical value keeps its sort real or
# complex, and the variants on number below have no C function: they only
# stand for the symbolic term.
SORT number
SUBSORT real,number
SUBSORT complex,number
# variables of sort number: they match terms of every sort below number
PAT _Anu,_Bnu,_Cnu,_Xnu,_Ynu,_Znu : number
# 2026: algebra, the sort of the elements of an associative algebra above
# number: its product need not be commutative (matrices, inc/linalg). Rules
# written for algebra hold for numbers as well; the rules for number (with
# a commutative product, like the integration) do not see the elements of
# algebra that are no numbers.
SORT algebra
SUBSORT number,algebra
PAT _Aal,_Bal,_Cal,_Xal,_Yal,_Zal : algebra

